    <div class="itq-answer" id="itqAns2">
      <h4>Answer (Logic + Code)</h4>
      <p>Use 3-reverse technique: reverse whole array, reverse first k, reverse rest.</p>
      <pre><code>public static void RotateRight(int[] slots, int k)
{
    if (slots == null) throw new ArgumentNullException(nameof(slots));
    int n = slots.Length;                                             // length
    if (n == 0) return;                                               // nothing to rotate

    k %= n;                                                           // normalize k
    if (k &lt; 0) k += n;                                                // handle negative k

    Reverse(slots, 0, n - 1);                                         // reverse all
    Reverse(slots, 0, k - 1);                                         // reverse first part
    Reverse(slots, k, n - 1);                                         // reverse remaining part
}</code></pre>
